<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chipata</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fort Jameson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chipata, called Fort Jameson until 1970, is a town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a> border. It was founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> around 1899 after the defeat of Mpezeni's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngoni">Ngoni</a> kingdom and named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leander-starr-jameson">Leander Starr Jameson</a>. It served as the capital of North-Eastern Rhodesia until the territory was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a> in 1911.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chipata.jpg" alt="Chipata" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dz217 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chipata_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
